Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:15:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/17] ttf: read each glyph's category as a shaper reads its
 class

The reader left every glyph's category unset, so a compiler guessed one from
the glyph's name: a gravecomb that the font's GDEF calls a base became a
zero-width mark, and so did an unencoded commaaccent in a font with no GDEF.

Categories now follow the GDEF glyph classes, or without them what a shaper
infers (a nonspacing-mark codepoint is a mark, anything else a base). A mark
is Nonspacing if it has no advance, else Spacing Combining, which keeps the
advance; a ligature's subcategory is Ligature. icu_properties (the version
glyphs-reader uses) gives the general category.

GdefClasses.ttf in the fixtures has GDEF classes; StaticLegacy.ttf has none.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
